      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a draft response that aims to address the concerns while maintaining a sincere and professional tone:\n\n\"We're deeply sorry to hear that our breakfast service fell short of your expectations this morning. We've taken notice of the complaints and are investigating the issues with cold food and long wait times for our guests. We also want to apologize for any frustration caused by our staff's demeanor, as we expect and deserve better ourselves. We'll be taking immediate action to improve our food quality and service, and we'll do our best to prevent situations like this from happening again in the future. Thank you for sharing your feedback, and we'll be in touch with a resolution plan.\"\n\nThis draft acknowledges the concerns, apologizes for the issues, and expresses a commitment to improvement. The tone is empathetic, yet professional, and avoids making excuses or justifying the poor service. The positivity score should be around 8-9, as it aims to be sincere, yet measured, in its apology and corrective measures.",
