      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised draft that maintains a professional tone while trying to shift the focus towards commitment to excellence and graciousness:\n\n\"We're so sorry to hear that our breakfast service didn't meet your expectations this morning. We value every guest who chooses to stay with us and are deeply grateful for the feedback that helps us grow and improve. We're taking immediate action to address the issues with cold food and long wait times, and we're committed to providing a warm welcome and exceptional service to all our guests. We're proud of our team's dedication to our guests' comfort and satisfaction, and we use every negative comment as an opportunity to learn and improve. Thanks for helping us get back on track, and we look forward to serving you better in the future.\"\n\nThis revised draft aims to present a more positive and gracious tone, focusing on the value of the client's feedback and the hotel's commitment to excellence. By framing the situation as an opportunity to learn and grow, the response shifts the focus away from criticism and towards the hotel's genuine interest in improving. The positivity score should bump up to around 12-13, which should clear the client's brand safety filters.",
